WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
A reading list gives new engineers no finish line,

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.880
so I end developer onboarding docs at a safe first merge.

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.360
Getting there takes one supported setup path with a check after each step,

4
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.100
because a clean exit only proves the command exited.

5
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.160
So when the health check fails,

6
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.340
the reader stops,

7
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.800
and the fix sits beside that command,

8
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.433
not in Slack.

9
00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:24.753
The first change is real and reversible,

10
00:00:24.813 --> 00:00:27.053
like rejecting an empty customer reference,

11
00:00:27.053 --> 00:00:30.273
with a test that fails first, then passes.

12
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.860
So after someone runs the route,

13
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.500
I'd note where they needed a rescue and fix that stage.
